hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"244","It is narrated by Bundar, it is narrated by Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Sulaym, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “He loved to take care of his affairs, even when he was walking, putting on his shoes, and purifying himself.”"
"245","On the authority of Ahmad bin Saeed Al-Darimi, on the authority of Abu Asim, on the authority of Hanzalah bin Abi Sufyan, who said: I heard Al-Qasim, saying: I heard Aisha, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to take a bath after milk, and he would take it with both hands and place it on his right side, and take it with both hands. He places it on his left side, then takes his hands and places it in the middle of his head.”"
